{% block how_it_works %}
## How it works

Run it before reading any metric. A mismatch between the arm sizes and the
planned split is an investigation alarm for allocation, logging or filtering;
it does not by itself identify a broken experiment.
`period="D"` repeats the check per day of assignment (`"W"` and `"M"` per week
and month, spelled as in `get_ab_test`), and `strata_col=` per segment fixed at
assignment; a segment computed after exposure is not a valid stratum here.
With `assignment=`, `segment_col` is optional: the table alone is counted.
SRM requires the coarsest declared path grain. A session-indexed assignment table does not
make repeated sessions of a user independent; finer-grain counts can be inspected
descriptively, without an allocation test. Declare a finer unit as primary only if the design
makes those units independent.

The caller must establish independent allocation with the specified probabilities.
Two-arm checks use `exact_binomial_two_sided` under `independent_bernoulli` allocation.
Multiarm checks use `pearson_chi_square_asymptotic` under `independent_multinomial`
allocation only when every expected arm count is at least five; this guard does not
make the approximation exact. Fixed-total and blocked designs require their own
diagnostic. An assignment roster alone does not establish the allocation model.

Explicit `expected_shares` keys define the planned arms, including arms with no
observed assignments. Unlisted observed arms remain in `unassigned_paths`.
Overall and split rows expose `p_value_method`, `sampling_assumption`,
`inference_status`, `support_warning`, and `expected_count_min`. `chi2` and `dof`
are descriptive Pearson quantities even when the p-value comes from the exact
binomial test. An unavailable check has `mismatch=None`, not a passing result;
`inference_status` must be `ok` to interpret its p-value. A conflicting assignment
still sets `mismatch=True` when the allocation test is unavailable.

Split rows form one planned Holm family, retaining unavailable groups in its
size. The overall check, separate calls and repeated looks are separate families.

The result's `reading` puts the check in one sentence: `"expected 50/50,
observed 5040/4960 (control/treatment), p 0.43: no mismatch"`, or
`"mismatch: ... — investigate allocation and logging before interpreting outcomes"` when the
split is off or paths carry two arms. With `strata_col=` or `period=` it also
names the strata or periods that mismatch: a logging bug on one platform can hide inside a plausible overall
split.
Sparse multiarm checks say `check unavailable`; they cannot be interpreted as
evidence that allocation passed.

